{
 "request_id": "gen-20261115T031048-ced865",
 "quotes": [
  {
   "id": "Q-1",
   "doc": "release_ex99_1.txt",
   "topic": "guidance",
   "text": "For the fourth quarter of 2026, AMD expects revenue to be approximately $17 billion, plus or minus 3%."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-2",
   "doc": "release_ex99_1.txt",
   "topic": "margin",
   "text": "Non-GAAP gross margin is expected to be approximately 55%."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-3",
   "doc": "release_ex99_1.txt",
   "topic": "demand",
   "text": "we expect growth to accelerate further in the fourth quarter as we scale Helios and ‘Venice’ production"
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-4",
   "doc": "release_ex99_1.txt",
   "topic": "demand",
   "text": "Our fourth-quarter outlook reflects accelerating revenue and earnings growth, driven by strong demand across our Data Center portfolio."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-5",
   "doc": "periodic.txt",
   "topic": "margin",
   "text": "Gross margin was 54% and 52% for the three months ended September 26, 2026 and September 27, 2025, respectively, where the increase was driven by a favorable product mix, including higher Data Center segment revenue."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-6",
   "doc": "periodic.txt",
   "topic": "risk",
   "text": "Government actions and regulations, including export controls, national-security-based regulations, import tariffs and trade protection measures, may limit our ability to export our products to certain customers, increase costs, harm our competitive position and materially affect our business."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-7",
   "doc": "periodic.txt",
   "topic": "other",
   "label": "one-off items",
   "text": "In addition, the tax benefit for the three and nine months ended September 26, 2026 also included a discrete tax benefit related to stock-based compensation of $772 million and $918 million, respectively."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-8",
   "doc": "periodic.txt",
   "topic": "other",
   "label": "one-off items",
   "text": "For the three and nine months ended September 26, 2026, we recorded an income tax benefit from continuing operations of $555 million and $65 million representing an effective tax rate of (29.6)% and (1.1)%, respectively."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-9",
   "doc": "periodic.txt",
   "topic": "other",
   "label": "one-off items",
   "text": "Other income (expense), net for the three months ended September 26, 2026 was $(902) million, a decrease of $984 million, compared to $82 million for the prior year period."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-10",
   "doc": "periodic.txt",
   "topic": "other",
   "label": "one-off items",
   "text": "The decrease in both periods was primarily driven by the change in fair value of warrant liability of $1.1 billion."
  },
  {
   "id": "Q-11",
   "doc": "periodic.txt",
   "topic": "other",
   "label": "one-off items",
   "text": "During the three and nine months ended September 26, 2026, the Company recorded a noncash charge of $1.2 billion, primarily related to a loss from remeasurement of the warrant liability based on the change in fair value of the warrants within Other income (expense), net."
  }
